 the MEMORY.md file, and it seems like I already got some content from my initial reading. I'll check if the file is in plain text. Whether to edit or overwrite is something I can decide once I inspect it. I want to craft a curated memory while ensuring nothing sensitive is included. It’s essential to make the sections durable, so I’ll focus on that as I proceed!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"장기적으로 남길 만한 항목만 추려 `MEMORY.md`를 정리합니다.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e9cc6f484c7ddde0169c31f3d5dec8191b1d350c63ca4904e\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_V21hFrTl8F0gC46RzoiojKNR|fc_0e9cc6f484c7ddde0169c31f3d66d4819198db80279f013c5d","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md","content":"# MEMORY.md — Curated Long-Term Memory\n\n## Workspace / Operating Patterns\n- OpenClaw workspace uses a file-memory pattern:\n  - daily notes in `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\n  - curated long-term memory in `MEMORY.md`\n  - operational state files such as `memory/heartbeat-state.json` and `memory/working-buffer.md`\n- A periodic memory-maintenance cron job is active and intended to distill recent daily notes back into this file.\n- The `using-superpowers` skill is treated as mandatory process guidance at session start; skill checking first is part of the operating discipline.\n\n## Automation / Cron\n- The system currently runs 8 active cron jobs; configuration was validated as healthy on 2026-03-25 after backup → write → validation.\n- Heartbeat automation exists as an isolated agentTurn cron routine driven by `HEARTBEAT.md`.\n- GitHub / daily briefing automations were adjusted to deliver Korean summaries for Sam.\n- A recurring morning daily-briefing automation exists around 08:32 KST, pulling Notion data and producing a concise Korean Telegram-oriented summary.\n\n## Important Operational Findings\n- Root cause identified for missing Telegram cron notifications in group chats:\n  - Telegram channel `groupPolicy` is `allowlist`\n  - allowlist is empty\n  - result: group messages, including cron completion notifications, are silently dropped\n- Recommended remediation path for that issue:\n  - populate the Telegram allowlist with authorized sender/group IDs, or\n  - change `groupPolicy` to `open` if that risk is acceptable\n- A transient `workspace-heartbeat` timeout occurred on 2026-03-16 and was confirmed recovered by 2026-03-17.\n\n## Ongoing Watch Items\n- `SESSION-STATE` has repeatedly indicated two unresolved watch items across multiple days:\n  - proactive loop implementation drift\n  - file-memory / semantic-memory alignment\n- Treat those as ongoing architectural hygiene items until explicitly resolved.\n\n## Tooling / Environment Notes\n- `gh api` does not support a `--limit` flag; avoid depending on it in GitHub CLI workflows.\n- The expected weather skill path was missing during a scheduled briefing run (`/home/lfant/.agents/skills/weather/SKILL.md` not found); weather-dependent automations may fail until the skill is installed or pathing is corrected.\n- A daily security audit cron exists and uses the healthcheck skill workflow for host/security review.\n\n## Curation Notes\n- Excluded repetitive low-signal entries (placeholder media prompts, repeated skill-invocation observations, routine heartbeat-state writes).\n- Keep this file focused on durable operating context, known failure modes, and active architectural concerns."},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md\",\"content\":\"# MEMORY.md — Curated Long-Term Memory\\n\\n## Workspace / Operating Patterns\\n- OpenClaw workspace uses a file-memory pattern:\\n  - daily notes in `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`\\n  - curated long-term memory in `MEMORY.md`\\n  - operational state files such as `memory/heartbeat-state.json` and `memory/working-buffer.md`\\n- A periodic memory-maintenance cron job is active and intended to distill recent daily notes back into this file.\\n- The `using-superpowers` skill is treated as mandatory process guidance at session start; skill checking first is part of the operating discipline.\\n\\n## Automation / Cron\\n- The system currently runs 8 active cron jobs; configuration was validated as healthy on 2026-03-25 after backup → write → validation.\\n- Heartbeat automation exists as an isolated agentTurn cron routine driven by `HEARTBEAT.md`.\\n- GitHub / daily briefing automations were adjusted to deliver Korean summaries for Sam.\\n- A recurring morning daily-briefing automation exists around 08:32 KST, pulling Notion data and producing a concise Korean Telegram-oriented summary.\\n\\n## Important Operational Findings\\n- Root cause identified for missing Telegram cron notifications in group chats:\\n  - Telegram channel `groupPolicy` is `allowlist`\\n  - allowlist is empty\\n  - result: group messages, including cron completion notifications, are silently dropped\\n- Recommended remediation path for that issue:\\n  - populate the Telegram allowlist with authorized sender/group IDs, or\\n  - change `groupPolicy` to `open` if that risk is acceptable\\n- A transient `workspace-heartbeat` timeout occurred on 2026-03-16 and was confirmed recovered by 2026-03-17.\\n\\n## Ongoing Watch Items\\n- `SESSION-STATE` has repeatedly indicated two unresolved watch items across multiple days:\\n  - proactive loop implementation drift\\n  - file-memory / semantic-memory alignment\\n- Treat those as ongoing architectural hygiene items until explicitly resolved.\\n\\n## Tooling / Environment Notes\\n- `gh api` does not support a `--limit` flag; avoid depending on it in GitHub CLI workflows.\\n- The expected weather skill path was missing during a scheduled briefing run (`/home/lfant/.agents/skills/weather/SKILL.md` not found); weather-dependent automations may fail until the skill is installed or pathing is corrected.\\n- A daily security audit cron exists and uses the healthcheck skill workflow for host/security review.\\n\\n## Curation Notes\\n-